Conclusion: exact-period Euler-copy capacity thickens the repeated tail by multiplicity pattern, but it is blind to QR/NQR within a fixed pattern because the unit packets are uniform over F_7^*.  The live extra coordinate is the quadratic-character phase moment.

========================================================================================
PAST-TOPIC INSPIRATION LEDGER
========================================================================================
Older repo threads suggest the right architecture here:
  residue/phase/incidence synthesis: copy mass is a residue capacity, quadratic character is a phase channel, and multi-large walls are an incidence/compatibility obligation;
  OCF packet lesson: retain packet address before scalar evaluation;
  root-packet lesson: closed packets need support plus incidence, not support alone;
  Burnside/totient/divisor ledgers: phi counts exact copies, but character channels decide how those copies cancel.

========================================================================================
TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS
========================================================================================
Pairwise observable: preservation of the signed k=10 coimage-tail predicate.
Switch: prefer the quotient that keeps residue multiplicity, copy capacity, and character phase with less raw row data.
Hamiltonian path:
  multi_large_residue_demand > quadratic_character_phase > euler_copy_unit_capacity > exact_period_1260_packets > height3_one_large_probe > raw_apex_mask > raw_runner_vertices
score_hist = {0:1,1:1,2:1,3:1,4:1,5:1,6:1}
